  "body": "**Scoped negative result; no new kappa.** Cross-block communication does not lower the complete helper-growth moment for the twelve fixed late interfaces in the selected PR1094 local word. For every 0 < s < 1, the exact minimum remains `328 + 56*2^s + 28*3^s + 20*4^s`, attained by the existing word.\n\nThis extends Ali Romman\u2019s #1429 at `591582004d82302268da3b264a6ba5edec1521de`, which excludes cross-block communication. The proof permits arbitrary finite rational mixing of all 96 helpers, input reassignment and repeated fixed-port reads. New global checks confine high dirty information and rank-seven cancellation frames. An actual simultaneous boundary and two modular rank witnesses establish independence of all 192 source/helper coordinates.\n\nScope is essential: fixed early source values and late target frames, monotone frames, 96 helpers, full rank-nine endpoints and an unchanged exterior. Extra arrays, later source versions, earlier output access and frame descents remain outside the result. The written all-length argument is distinct from its finite premise checks; no full multiplication theorem, new supplier, native/global admission or selected cold replay is claimed.\n\nReproduce with Python 3.12 and the standard library:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/complex-cross-block-locality\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/complex-cross-block-locality outcome=negative-result`.\n\nValidation passed: source/Git pins; all 3060 local supports; 4560 input-frame pairs; 1056 foreign high/input and 4608 input/target checks; 24 cancellation frames; a separate set/integer-minor implementation with 240 scalar columns and boundary rank 192 over two primes; 12 built-in rejection controls; four corruption/read-only relocation tests; optimized Python 3.14 replays; selected-record and whitespace checks. The two implementations are by the same assisted author, not independent human review. Hosted CI status is separate.\n\nExact base: `ef5f39403610d231a0c27e8a6b4f08c10209bcd6`. OS assignment seed 33. Only `research/complex-cross-block-locality/` is added. Its README, proof and manifests contain the complete scope, immutable source identities, open next question and predecessor attribution. No frontier or frozen source changes.\n\nCredit Ali Romman for the inherited block extractor and carrier/retirement arguments; Jeremy Kothe, Rohan Arun, Hao Yan, icekylinx, Chafik Boukhalfa, Jonathan Capalbo and the retained construction lineage. Prepared for Hanson Sun (@bbMisk) with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in derivation, code, proof, checks and writing; Apache-2.0.\n\nCoordination: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1492\n",
